      "message": "In our ko, we added mem_cgroup_commit_charge_batch, which is similar to mem_cgroup_commit_charge, but it processes a batch of folios.\n\nThe pseudo code of mem_cgroup_commit_charge_batch is as follows.\n```\nmem_cgroup_commit_charge_batch()\n{\n\tunsigned long nr_memory \u003d 0;\n\tfor ( /* Iterate over the folio list */) {\n\t\tif (/* Special judgments in ko */ )\n\t\t\tcontinue;\n  \n\t\tcommit_charge(folio, memcg); /* set folio-\u003ememcg_data here */\n\t\tnr_memory++; /* +1 because it\u0027s not a large folio */\n\t}\n\tcss_get_many(\u0026memcg-\u003ecss, nr_memory);\n\tmemcg1_charge_batch(memcg, nr_memory, 0); /* !NUMA */\n}\n```\n\nWe copy the implementation of commit_charge and call it to set folio-\u003ememcg_data.\nThe reason why we did not add mem_cgroup_commit_charge_batch to mm/memcontrol.c is that the folio batch is not a simple list and additional judgments need to be made on it. (Because this is not universal, adding callback functions to the parameters is also considered ugly).\n\nIn addition, we also called a function similar to try_charge before calling mem_cgroup_commit_charge_batch.\n\nIn summary, only the clear and simple memcg1_charge_batch is added.",
